course: dictionary
lesson: 12680
title: Distributed: given out and spread out
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Distributed means given out or shared among people or places. When a teacher hands out papers to the class, she has distributed them. The word can also mean spread out over an area, like seeds that have been scattered across a field.
explain: Look at the words around distributed to find its meaning. «The teacher distributed the spelling lists to every child.» The words every child tell you the lists were given out to lots of people. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: In maths, distributed often means shared out equally. «The 24 sweets were distributed equally among 4 friends.» Each friend gets 24 ÷ 4, which is 6 sweets. The clue equally tells you the sharing is fair, with nobody getting more than anyone else.
fact: Distributed means given out or shared among people or groups.
fact: Distributed can also mean spread out over an area, like seeds spread across a field.
fact: «Distributed» is a form of the verb distribute: distribute, distributes, distributed, distributing.
fact: Wind and animals can distribute seeds, carrying them far away from the parent plant.
fact: Synonyms for distributed include given out, shared out and spread out, but each one fits some sentences better than others.
exercise: «The teacher distributed the spelling lists to every child.» What does distributed mean here? | Written on the board | Lost in the classroom | Collected and thrown away | *Gave out to each child
exercise: «The 24 sweets were distributed equally among 4 friends.» How many sweets does each friend get? | *6 | 20 | 8 | 4
exercise: «The wind distributed the dandelion seeds across the whole field.» What does distributed suggest? | Burned to ash | Gathered into one small pile | Counted one by one | *Spread out over a wide area
test: «Food was distributed to families in need at the church hall.» What does distributed mean? | *Given out to people who needed it | Hidden under the table | Thrown away at the end of the day
test: «The results were distributed across three groups.» What does distributed mean here? | Written in red ink | Added up into one total | *Spread out among the groups
exam: Which word means the same as distributed in «The papers were distributed to the class»? | *Given out | Counted | Hidden | Torn
